    "body": "pulse task #2887 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:6028b757889ce7591cf1c6e08322a5b7 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2887: Handle unsafe local CI step IDs without log-path failures\n\nOperation: 6028b757889ce7591cf1c6e08322a5b7\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nFocused pre-existing runner defect discovered during Main effects #2882 / PR484 validation. Keep separate from frozen process-optimization #2886 / PR487; this is not a new blocker for that candidate. Live duplicate searches for log, step and filename found no matching focused issue.\n\nEvidence: Main component session79088 passed its seven cheap checks, then failed before the first Cargo command because the custom step ID `transport/routes` was interpolated directly into a log filename. The owning agent changed only its private orchestration label and continued. Raw traceback/partial summary are retained under #2882 note30628. Current published source3111b27f563350ac38294943c8d4f5caca7f1173 has the same existing `_run_step` behavior in scripts/local-ci.py: `output_dir / f\"{index:02d}-{step.step_id}.log\"`. FileNotFoundError handling then tries to write to the same invalid path and can escape again, confusing log-path failure with a missing executable.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Define and enforce a finite filename-safe step-ID contract before execution, or derive a bounded safe filename independently while preserving the original step ID in the certificate. Do not permit path traversal, unintended directories, collisions or writes outside the run output directory.\n- Invalid IDs produce an explicit controlled refusal and truthful incomplete/failed summary; no command runs and target locks/signal handlers are released normally. Do not report the invalid log path as a missing required executable or mark any test passed.\n- Preserve valid existing run IDs, log/certificate linkage and scoped/full qualification behavior. Do not weaken required test counts or source/cache ownership laws.\n- Use focused Python fixtures for normal IDs, separator/dot-dot inputs and a genuine missing executable. No Cargo/native build is needed for this path-only runner repair.\n\nCanonical source: https://github.com/PORTALSURFER/hex/blob/3111b27f563350ac38294943c8d4f5caca7f1173/scripts/local-ci.py . Main work and current final CI continue independently.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
